🚀 Agent run completed. Output: ## Factor Mining Cycle — 2026-12-17

### Explored Factors

Tested two interpretable factor families across the 15 tradable benchmark instruments, using only completed observations through 2026-12-16 and next-day close-to-close returns:

1. **Common-factor-neutral momentum**
   - Signal: each instrument’s trailing \(h\)-day return minus the cross-sectional median trailing return.
   - Windows tested: 20, 40, 60, and 120 trading days.
   - Motivation: isolate relative momentum from broad benchmark direction.

2. **Volatility-adjusted reversal**
   - Signal: negative trailing return divided by trailing realized volatility.
   - Configurations tested: 3d/20d, 5d/20d, 5d/60d, and 10d/60d.
   - Motivation: distinguish economically meaningful reversals from moves occurring during unusually high volatility.

### Validation Results

| Factor | Dates | Avg. instruments | Daily IC | Daily ICIR | Hit ratio | Rank turnover | Result |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Common-neutral momentum 20d | 1,414 | 14.11 | −0.016400 | −0.044996 | 47.17% | 0.1112 | Failed |
| Common-neutral momentum 40d | 1,077 | 14.13 | −0.005036 | −0.013909 | 48.75% | 0.0902 | Failed |
| Common-neutral momentum 60d | 736 | 14.08 | −0.005452 | −0.014870 | 47.96% | 0.0873 | Failed |
| Common-neutral momentum 120d | 1,023 | 14.08 | +0.004336 | +0.011315 | 50.44% | 0.0565 | Failed |
| Vol-adjusted reversal 3d/20d | 92 | 14.03 | +0.005445 | +0.016043 | 53.26% | 0.1862 | Failed |
| Vol-adjusted reversal 5d/20d | 92 | 14.03 | +0.045884 | +0.152814 | 56.52% | 0.1522 | Not admitted |
| Vol-adjusted reversal 5d/60d | 52 | 14.06 | −0.018700 | −0.059732 | 48.08% | 0.1428 | Failed |
| Vol-adjusted reversal 10d/60d | 52 | 14.06 | +0.026200 | +0.076545 | 53.85% | 0.1093 | Not admitted |

The benchmark admission thresholds are absolute daily IC ≥ 0.0070 and absolute daily ICIR ≥ 0.0840. Although the 5d/20d and 10d/60d volatility-adjusted reversal variants exceeded or approached both numerical thresholds, they were supported only by 92 and 52 observations, respectively, all concentrated in 2026. They therefore lack multi-regime validation and were not admitted.

The common-neutral momentum family failed the ICIR threshold across every tested window. The 20d version was consistently negative, including negative results in six of the seven calendar years.

