| Dispersion-conditioned common-neutralized reversal | 5d | 4,128 | 14.82 | 0.02772 | 0.08032 | Below ICIR gate |
| Dispersion-conditioned common-neutralized reversal | 10d | 4,123 | 14.82 | 0.00431 | 0.01252 | Failed |

The common-neutralized factor passed the absolute IC threshold but failed the required daily ICIR threshold of 0.0840. Its recent-period daily ICIR also weakened to approximately 0.063 during July 2026–February 2027.

The dispersion-conditioned version reproduced the existing graded dispersion-reversal results almost exactly because the common activation scalar does not materially change cross-sectional ranking. It is therefore not an independent candidate.

Coverage was approximately 98.8% by factor-date cross-section for the common-neutralized test. Rank turnover was 0.18035. The signal artifact was generated at:

`../persistent/factor_signals_miner_2_20270225_neutral_dispersion_reversal.csv`

`max_abs_library_correlation` was unavailable; deterministic post-Miner correlation recomputation remains authoritative.

