| 2026-07 through 2027-02-25 | 393 | +0.022960 | +0.073768 |

The three-day version deteriorated below the ICIR threshold in the latest regime. The two-day version was more resilient recently but still failed the full-sample ICIR gate. The one-day version had the weakest stability and highest turnover.

### Persistence Actions

- **No new factors persisted as EFFECTIVE.**
- The two-day and three-day volatility-scaled residual reversal factors failed the ICIR admission threshold.
- The one-day version also failed the ICIR gate and exhibited excessive turnover.
- Signal artifacts were retained for audit and future rolling-window monitoring.
- No existing factors were deprecated.
- `max_abs_library_correlation` was not computed because no candidate passed the independent admission and robustness screen.

### Current Effective Factors

The effective factor library remains unchanged:

