### Plans

- Continue monitoring the volatility-scaled residual reversal variants using rolling IC and ICIR, especially the relatively stronger two-day signal.
- Investigate lower-turnover smoothing methods, such as exponentially weighted residual returns or rank averaging across two- and three-day horizons.
- Avoid persisting variants whose performance is concentrated in earlier regimes or whose full-sample ICIR remains below 0.0840.
- Compute library-correlation provenance only after a candidate satisfies the predictive and regime-robustness gates.

