### Explored Factors

1. **Volatility-Impulse Reversal**
   - Construction:  
     \[
     -\left(\frac{\text{5-day realized volatility}}{\text{30-day realized volatility}}-1\right)
     \]
   - Interpretation: assets experiencing a volatility surge are expected to mean-revert.
   - Cross-sectional, long-only compatible, and based solely on lagged returns.

2. **Path-Efficiency Reversal**
   - Construction: rolling signed return divided by rolling absolute-return path length:
     \[
     \frac{\sum r_t}{\sum |r_t|}
     \]
   - Tested 10-, 20-, 30-, and 60-day windows.
   - Interpretation: highly directional price paths may be vulnerable to subsequent reversal.

### Validation Results

| Factor | Horizon | Dates | Avg. instruments | IC | ICIR | Hit rate | Coverage / Turnover |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Volatility impulse | 1d | 2,440 | 11.96 | -0.00136 | -0.00482 | 50.1% | 46.6% / 0.108 |
| Volatility impulse | 5d | 2,436 | 11.96 | -0.00141 | -0.00502 | 49.1% | 46.6% / 0.108 |
| Volatility impulse | 10d | 2,431 | 11.96 | -0.00359 | -0.01296 | 50.1% | 46.6% / 0.108 |
| Path efficiency, 10d | 1d | 113 | 11.14 | -0.04736 | -0.14114 | 40.7% | 16.1% / 0.167 |
| Path efficiency, 20d | 1d | 103 | 11.16 | -0.06356 | -0.20512 | 38.8% | 15.8% / 0.188 |
| Path efficiency, 30d | 1d | 93 | 11.17 | -0.08461 | -0.25716 | 39.8% | 15.5% / 0.179 |
| Path efficiency, 60d | 1d | 63 | 11.25 | -0.07094 | -0.23614 | 41.3% | 14.6% / 0.182 |

The volatility-impulse candidate failed the benchmark admission gates of absolute IC ≥ 0.0070 and absolute ICIR ≥ 0.0840 at all tested horizons.

Path efficiency showed strong negative predictive power in the available recent sample, especially at longer forward horizons, but the artifact contained only 63–113 valid dates and approximately 15–16% average universe coverage due to the available data window. The result was therefore not considered sufficiently robust for admission across historical regimes. No library-correlation value was persisted because the candidate failed the primary robustness decision.

