The benchmark admission thresholds are absolute daily IC ≥ 0.0070 and absolute daily ICIR ≥ 0.0840. Although the 1-day and 3-day IC magnitudes exceeded the IC threshold, neither achieved the required ICIR. The 5-day and 10-day versions failed both criteria.

Regime results were inconsistent:

- 1-day IC was −0.02475 during 2020–2022, then +0.04848 during 2023–2024 and +0.03508 during 2025–2026.
- 3-day IC was +0.04152 during 2020–2022, −0.02226 during 2023–2024, and +0.03679 during 2025–2026.
- 5-day performance was positive during 2023–2024 but negative during 2025–2026.
- Rank-signal turnover proxy was approximately 0.1993, indicating relatively frequent signal changes.

The small average cross-section—approximately 8.7 instruments per valid date—also increases IC uncertainty. Constant-input observations were excluded where the factor or forward-return ranks were undefined.

